  "name": "luh-uct-data-from-a-parameter-study-on-316l-cucrzr-multi-material-specimens",
  "notes": "This dataset was generated in the context of a parameter study in the paper:\r\n_Supplementary data of “Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – Influence of process parameters on interface formation in in-plane 316L/CuCrZr laser powder bed fusion\"_ \r\n\r\nIt includes data of CT-scans of 14 specimens with the following sample number: 1, 8, 10, 15 (3x), 16, 24, 25, 26, 31, 32, 33, 40.\r\n\r\n* __Materials:__ 316L (Carpenter Additive) and CuCrZr (Eckart TLS GmbH)\r\n* __PBF-LB Machine:__ Aconity MIDI+ equipped with an integrated Aerosint SPD Recoater V1.0\r\n* __µCT Scanner:__ Bruker SkyScan 1275\r\n* __Result Image Width:__ 1944 pixels\r\n* __Result Image Height:__ 1944 pixels\r\n\r\n![ Exemplary computed tomography image of a 316L/CuCrZr multi-material sample (Sample 1)](https://data.uni-hannover.de/de/dataset/fb2dd8d5-ff72-4e73-bb6d-e942b3c288f6/resource/db9251a0-4a7a-443e-b51e-d21b0f2ce788/download/exemplary_ct_sample_1.jpg)\r\nExemplary computed tomography image of a 316L/CuCrZr multi-material sample (Sample 1)\r\n\r\n### References\r\n\r\nMeyer, I., Oel, M., Ehlers, T., & Lachmayer, R. (2023). *Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – Design guidelines for manufacturing of 316L/CuCrZr in laser powder bed fusion*. Heliyon, 9(8), e18301. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2023.e18301\r\n\r\nIna Meyer, Cameron Owen Messmann, Roland Lachmayer (2026). *CT-based porosity analysis of 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/wzrn3izc\r\n\r\nIna Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *Additive manufacturing data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/7p6wv6cg\r\n\r\nIna Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *Light microscopy data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/rsjz3w2k\r\n\r\nIna Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *SEM data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/wan2sabi\r\n\r\n### Acknowledgments\r\n\r\nThe project ”*Additive Fertigung multimaterieller Komponenten zur nachhaltigen Energiewandlung*” was funded by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF) and the state of Lower Saxony – Project number ZW 7-87011865.\r\n\r\nThe project ”*Major Research Instrumentation for integration of efficient effects in multi-material structural components*” was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG - German Research Foundation) - Project number 445707542.\r\n",
